 "docs": {
  "en": {
   "title": "Where should you ski in the US West this weekend? Telluride, Wolf Creek and Purgatory Resort",
   "description": "Where should you go skiing in the US West? Three inputs, one shortlist: today's snow depth, the new snow of the last 72 hours and the forecast point …",
   "lede": "Where should you go skiing in the US West? Three inputs, one shortlist: today's snow depth, the new snow of the last 72 hours and the forecast point to Telluride, Wolf Creek and Purgatory Resort. Top of this list: Wolf Creek, about 34 in (87 cm) up high. Then Telluride 34 in (86 cm) and Purgatory Resort 22 in (57 cm). Confidence: good for the trend, lower for any single number.",
   "sections": [
    {
     "h": "The forecast in short",
     "p": [
      "Next round by 14 November: 4 in (9 cm) at Telluride, 3 in (8 cm) at Wolf Creek and 5 in (12 cm) at Purgatory Resort, according to our forecast.",
      "Forecasts a few days ahead can change: look at the map again the day before you travel."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Top and bottom are two different worlds",
     "p": [
      "The top of Telluride has about 38 in (96 cm) at 12,507 ft (3,812 m), the bottom about 0 in (0 cm) at 8,734 ft (2,662 m).",
      "Ski the upper lifts and plan to ride down by lift if the lower runs are thin.",
      "At about 10,620 ft (3,237 m), Telluride has 8 in (20 cm) today; a normal 11 November has 9 in (24 cm) there.",
      "That is more than in 21 of the 46 past winters on this date.",
      "In past winters the best snow at Telluride usually came early January / early March.",
      "Height by height at Telluride: 8,734 ft (2,662 m) 0 in (0 cm) on the ground, 2 in (6 cm) more in the next 7 days; 10,620 ft (3,237 m) 2 in (6 cm) on the ground, 6 in (15 cm) more in the next 7 days; 12,507 ft (3,812 m) 38 in (96 cm) on the ground, 7 in (19 cm) more in the next 7 days."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Snow line check",
     "p": [
      "On 11 November the freezing level at Telluride sits at 11,483 ft (3,500 m) to 13,484 ft (4,110 m), over the top of the resort (12,507 ft / 3,812 m): rain or wet snow could fall on all slopes.",
      "A rule of thumb that is rarely wrong: high and north-facing keeps snow, south-facing loses it first."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Top choices",
     "p": [
      "Telluride by height, from our model: top 38 in (96 cm) (12,507 ft / 3,812 m), middle 2 in (6 cm) (10,620 ft / 3,237 m), base 0 in (0 cm) (8,734 ft / 2,662 m). Telluride: snow-covered in the last clear view, on 9 November.",
      "Three heights at Wolf Creek, three numbers: 19 in (47 cm) at the top (11,762 ft / 3,585 m), 15 in (37 cm) at mid-mountain (11,010 ft / 3,356 m), 3 in (8 cm) at the base (10,262 ft / 3,128 m). Clear sky over Wolf Creek on 3 November, and the image shows snow cover.",
      "Purgatory Resort: snow-covered in the last clear view, on 9 November."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Avalanche danger and safety",
     "p": [
      "The official rating for the Telluride area is 1 on the 5-level scale today (Colorado Avalanche Information Center).",
      "Before you ski off-piste or go touring, read the official avalanche bulletin (links below)."
     ]
    }
   ],
   "advice": [
    "Snow on the map does not mean a resort is open: check lifts and opening dates on the resort's website.",
    "Small ski areas next to the big names often get the same storm and shorter lift lines. Check them on the map first.",
    "Early-season snow is thin. Stay on open, groomed pistes: rocks and grass can hide just under the surface.",
    "Satellite images show it every winter: snow stays longest high up and on north-facing slopes, and goes first on south-facing ones.",
    "Get a powder alert in the SnowScope app to know when Telluride gets fresh snow."
   ],
   "captions": {
    "alt_sat": "Snow depth in the US West on 11 November 2026 (SnowScope snow model): Telluride, Wolf Creek, Purgatory Resort, Brian Head Resort.",
    "map": "Snow depth in the US West on 11 November 2026 (SnowScope snow model): Telluride, Wolf Creek, Purgatory Resort, Brian Head Resort."
   }
  }
